<article class="env-lemma" id="09L0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09L0">Lemma <span data-tag="09L0">22.23.1</span>.</a> Let $(A, \text{d})$ be a differential graded algebra. The functor $\text{Mod}_{(A, \text{d})} \to D(A, \text{d})$ defined has the natural structure of a $\delta $-functor, with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \delta _{K \to L \to M} = - p \circ q^{-1}  \]
</div>
  <p> with $p$ and $q$ as explained above. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have already seen that this choice leads to a distinguished triangle whenever given a short exact sequence of complexes. We have to show functoriality of this construction, see Derived Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/0150" data-tag="0150">13.3.6</a>. This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/09KD" data-tag="09KD">22.6.2</a> with a bit of work. Compare with Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0152" data-tag="0152">13.12.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>